The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.


Short description
-----------------

extrudate_swell1:

 Extrudate swell problem of a Newtonian fluid (Stokes)
 Optionally include surface tension (using an object).
 Planar or axisymmetrical flow

extrudate_swell2:

 Viscoelastic extrudate swell problem
 Planar flow for a UCM/Oldroyd-B model
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order Gear time integration

extrudate_swell3:

 Viscoelastic extrudate swell problem
 Axisymmetrical flow for a Giesekus model
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order Gear time integration

extrudate_swell4:

 Extrudate swell problem of a Newtonian fluid (Stokes)
 Planar or axisymmetrical flow
 XFEM approach
 Optionally include surface tension

extrudate_swell5:

 Viscoelastic extrudate swell problem
 Planar flow for a UCM/Oldroyd-B model
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 XFEM approach
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 second-order Gear time integration
 Optionally include surface tension

extrudate_swell6:

 Extrudate swell problem of a Newtonian fluid (Stokes)
 Optionally include surface tension (using a curve).
 Planar or axisymmetrical flow
 This problem is similar to extrudate_swell1, but now implemented using a
 more simple approach of using a boundary integral on a curve.

extrudate_swell7:

 3D extrudate swell problem of a Newtonian fluid (Stokes).
 Die is a square and contains sharp edges.
 Free surfaces are expanded according to the movement of material lines.

extrudate_swell8:

 3D extrudate swell problem of a viscoelastic fluid.
 DEVSS-G/SUPG
 Optional DEVSS. If DEVSS is not used, the G-method is still used
 Implicit bilinear terms of CE in momentum balance.
 Second-order Gear time integration.
 This problem is similar to extrudate_swell7, but now for
 a viscoelastic fluid.
